.TH LD 1 "July 4, 2026" "ReBSD"
.SH NAME
ld \- ReBSD MIPS link editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ld
[
.B \-sSxXrdtv
]
[
.B \-EL
|
.B \-EB
]
[
.B \-\-sysroot
.I dir
|
.BI \-\-sysroot= dir
]
[
.B \-L
.I dir
]
[
.B \-o
.I file
]
[
.B \-l
.I name
]
[
.B \-u
.I name
]
[
.B \-e
.I name
]
[
.BI \-T address
]
.I file
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ld
combines ReBSD
.B a.out
object files and archives into an executable or relocatable output file.
It resolves external references, searches archive libraries, writes MIPS
relocation records when needed, and emits the ReBSD
.B a.out
format used by the native toolchain.
.PP
The default output file is
.IR a.out .
Archive libraries are searched at the point where they appear on the
command line.
Libraries indexed by
.BR ranlib (1)
contain a
.B __.SYMDEF
member that lets
.B ld
load archive members needed to satisfy unresolved references.
.PP
The linker defines the standard end symbols
.BR _etext ,
.BR _edata ,
.BR _end ,
and their C names
.BR etext ,
.BR edata ,
and
.BR end .
It also defines the constructor and destructor range symbols used by the
ReBSD C runtime.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " file"
Write the output to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-L " dir"
Add
.I dir
to the library search path.
All
.B \-L
directories are collected before any
.B \-l
library is resolved, so compiler drivers may place default library
directories after user objects.
.TP
.BI \-\-sysroot " dir"
.TQ
.BI \-\-sysroot= dir
Use
.I dir
as the root for standard library directories.
The default sysroot is
.IR / .
Explicit
.B \-L
directories are used as written.
.TP
.BI \-l " name"
Search for
.BI lib name .a
in the library search path.
The standard library directories are
.IR /lib ,
.IR /usr/lib ,
and
.IR /usr/local/lib ,
under the selected sysroot.
.TP
.BI \-u " symbol"
Enter
.I symbol
as an initially undefined symbol.
This is useful when linking only from libraries.
.TP
.BI \-e " symbol"
Use
.I symbol
as the output entry point.
If no entry point is specified, the target default text base is used.
.TP
.BI \-T address
Set the text segment base address.
The target default is selected when
.B ld
is built.
.TP
.B \-EL
Read and write little\-endian
.B a.out
objects.
.TP
.B \-EB
Read and write big\-endian
.B a.out
objects.
.TP
.B \-r
Produce relocatable output and preserve relocation records.
Undefined symbols are allowed in relocatable output.
.TP
.B \-d
Force common symbols to be allocated even when relocatable output is
requested.
.TP
.B \-s
Strip all symbols from final output.
.TP
.B \-S
Discard non\-loadable absolute and debug\-like symbols while retaining the
symbols needed by normal toolchain output.
.TP
.B \-x
Discard local symbols.
.TP
.B \-X
Discard local symbols whose names start with
.B L
or
.BR . .
.TP
.B \-t
Increase trace verbosity.
This option may be repeated for more detailed linker diagnostics.
.TP
.B \-v
Enable verbose linker diagnostics.
.TP
.B \-\-fatal\-warnings
Accepted for compiler\-driver compatibility.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I a.out
Default output file.
.TP
.I /lib/lib*.a
Standard libraries.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/lib*.a
Standard libraries.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/lib*.a
Standard libraries.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR as (1),
.BR cc (1),
.BR pcc (1),
.BR ranlib (1),
.BR nm (1),
.BR size (1),
.BR a.out (5)
